cpuidle: psci: Initialize after the deferred probes.

The psci-cpuidle faux device probes once, at device_initcall. With the
MPM as the parent of both CPU cluster domains, the PSCI domains defer
until the MPM probes and arrive only from the deferred probe work. So
the cpuidle driver found no domain ("CPU 0 failed to PSCI idle") and
the CPUs only ever ran WFI. late_initcall_sync comes after
deferred_probe_initcall has run and flushed them.

--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -489,4 +489,9 @@
 
 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+/*
+ * The faux device probes once. The CPU PM domains may still wait for a
+ * parent domain (the MPM on SM6115 and QCM2290) and come only from the
+ * deferred probes, which late_initcall runs and waits for.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
